{"file": "D:\\SpaceBook\\_cls6_jpg\\geo\\048.jpg", "lines": [{"text": "C.Climatesof PolarZone", "conf": 0.892, "box": [[64, 119], [419, 114], [419, 147], [65, 151]]}, {"text": "There are three types of polar climates. These include the subarctic climate, the tundra.", "conf": 0.943, "box": [[63, 175], [1198, 162], [1198, 198], [64, 211]]}, {"text": "climate, and the polar icecap climate. Tundra climate has been explained here in brief.", "conf": 0.933, "box": [[63, 215], [1076, 200], [1076, 239], [64, 254]]}, {"text": "I)Tundra", "conf": 0.801, "box": [[65, 273], [178, 266], [180, 300], [67, 307]]}, {"text": "The tundra is a treeless plain located in the northernmost part of the Earth. It is a cold desert", "conf": 0.948, "box": [[65, 323], [1185, 308], [1186, 344], [66, 359]]}, {"text": "and is a desolate land covered with lakes, ponds and marshes. Permafrost is an important", "conf": 0.938, "box": [[65, 359], [1186, 347], [1186, 386], [66, 398]]}, {"text": "featureofthis climate.", "conf": 0.896, "box": [[69, 405], [336, 397], [337, 424], [70, 432]]}, {"text": "Precipitation is light and it takes place in the form of snow. Average annual precipitation is", "conf": 0.943, "box": [[68, 530], [1184, 519], [1184, 555], [69, 567]]}, {"text": "about200mm.", "conf": 0.835, "box": [[69, 574], [241, 569], [242, 598], [70, 602]]}, {"text": "120°E", "conf": 0.622, "box": [[911, 619], [972, 619], [972, 643], [911, 643]]}, {"text": "30°W", "conf": 0.644, "box": [[500, 620], [554, 620], [554, 645], [500, 645]]}, {"text": "30°E", "conf": 0.648, "box": [[668, 620], [718, 620], [718, 645], [668, 645]]}, {"text": "60°E", "conf": 0.732, "box": [[750, 620], [802, 620], [802, 645], [750, 645]]}, {"text": "90°E", "conf": 0.683, "box": [[832, 620], [882, 620], [882, 645], [832, 645]]}, {"text": "150°E", "conf": 0.693, "box": [[994, 617], [1055, 617], [1055, 641], [994, 641]]}, {"text": "120°W", "conf": 0.635, "box": [[254, 622], [315, 620], [316, 644], [255, 646]]}, {"text": "90\"W", "c